# usefullscreen branch — auto push & Vercel deploy

When you finish implementing user-requested code changes on branch `usefullscreen`, **automatically** commit, push, and deploy to Vercel without waiting for the user to ask again.

## Workflow (run after every successful change)

1. Verify build: `npm run build:vercel`
2. Commit with a concise message (HEREDOC). Use git author env vars if local git identity is unset:
   - `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=dylanaidev-hub`
   - `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=dylanaidev-hub@users.noreply.github.com`
   - Same for `GIT_COMMITTER_*`
3. Push: `git push origin usefullscreen`
4. Deploy production:
   ```bash
   NPM_CONFIG_CACHE=/tmp/npm-cache-vercel npx --yes vercel@54.14.2 deploy --prod --yes
   ```

## Targets

- **Branch:** `usefullscreen`
- **Production URL:** https://doihinhsanco-usefullscreen.vercel.app/app
- **Vercel project:** `doihinhsanco-usefullscreen` (team `lineup-football`)
- **Build command:** `npm run build:vercel` (via `vercel.json`)

## Skip auto deploy only when

- User explicitly says not to commit, push, or deploy
- Build fails — fix first, then run the full workflow
- No code changes were made (question-only / review-only tasks)

## After deploy

Briefly confirm: commit SHA, production URL, and inspect link if useful.
